WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.145
Your next service starts long before the first plate.

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:09.565
Start with your menu, type or paste dishes,

00:00:09.805 --> 00:00:13.585
upload photos, or use a website link you have permission to
import.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:20.005
Using your phone, scan the code to send menu photos straight to

00:00:20.005 --> 00:00:20.545
your workspace.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.385
Here, we'll read a photo.

00:00:26.185 --> 00:00:29.585
Check the extracted text, review ingredient quantities and
units,

00:00:29.905 --> 00:00:30.905
then approve your menu.

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:41.435
Need another supplier?

00:00:42.135 --> 00:00:43.415
Choose an ingredient and area,

00:00:43.775 --> 00:00:45.235
then search external websites.

00:00:45.975 --> 00:00:48.135
Review the listing before adding their details.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.055
Already have trusted contacts?

00:00:52.695 --> 00:00:53.395
Add them directly.

00:00:54.055 --> 00:00:56.295
Your restaurant supplier records stay private.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.925
Create one price request with quantities,

00:01:03.145 --> 00:01:05.505
delivery timing, and a deadline for replies.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.275
New suppliers can apply.

00:01:09.895 --> 00:01:12.935
Your team reviews each application and decides who can quote.

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:20.485
They send their prices through a private link.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.055
Compare the full cost.

00:01:28.675 --> 00:01:31.795
Here, a lower price per kilo costs more after delivery.

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:44.465
Choose one supplier for the whole request,

00:01:44.765 --> 00:01:46.505
or split the purchase by item.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.715
For this order, choose one supplier and save the purchasing
decision.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.300
Check each delivery against the quantities you awarded.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:05.660
Record everything received, separate rejected items, and
enter billed quantities

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:06.320
and rates.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:10.580
Partial deliveries stay visible until the remaining
quantities arrive.

00:02:13.527 --> 00:02:14.907
Keep money owed in view.

00:02:15.787 --> 00:02:19.627
Record the credit claimed, how much has been received, and
the settlement reference.

00:02:20.567 --> 00:02:23.747
Update these recorded amounts when the supplier settles the
balance.

00:02:26.553 --> 00:02:30.913
Supplier performance brings accepted quantities, rejection
rates, delivery

00:02:30.913 --> 00:02:33.033
dates, and outstanding credits together.

00:02:33.813 --> 00:02:36.173
Missing checks never count as successful deliveries.

00:02:37.293 --> 00:02:39.073
Limited history is clearly labeled.

00:02:41.767 --> 00:02:44.347
Before the next service, choose an approved menu.

00:02:45.367 --> 00:02:49.927
Enter the servings each recipe batch makes, your planned
portions, usable stock,

00:02:50.307 --> 00:02:51.107
and expected yield.

00:02:51.967 --> 00:02:54.907
Add incoming supplies only when their arrival is confirmed.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:01.720
Here, the kitchen needs 10 kilos, with 4 kilos already
usable.

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:07.120
At 80% yield, the remaining 6 kilos require a 7.5

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:07.840
kilo purchase.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:10.200
Shared stock is counted once.

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:15.340
Create a purchase draft for the missing ingredients.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.880
Review suppliers and delivery terms before sending.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:23.040
Repeat the daily plan for another service with fresh stock
counts.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.215
Next time, open your history.

00:03:28.995 --> 00:03:30.535
Repeat the purchase as a new draft.

00:03:31.295 --> 00:03:33.195
Update the dates and review it before sending.

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:41.445
QuotePlate. Keep every purchase clear.
